{
  "title": "The while Loop — Repeating Until a Condition Is Met",
  "subtitle": "Dynamic Condition-Driven Loops & Infinite Loop Prevention",
  "topic": "5.2 • THE WHILE LOOP",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      5.2 • Conditional Iteration\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>while</hlt> Loop\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Unlike for loops which run a set number of times, a <code>while</code> loop keeps repeating as long as its condition remains <strong>True</strong>!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      The 3 Requirements of a while Loop\n    </span>\n    <ol style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; margin-left: 20px; line-height: 1.6;\">\n      <li><strong>Initial State:</strong> Create a variable before the loop (e.g. <code>count = 1</code>).</li>\n      <li><strong>Loop Condition:</strong> The check that keeps it going (e.g. <code>while count &lt;= 3:</code>).</li>\n      <li><strong>Update Step:</strong> Modify the variable inside the loop (e.g. <code>count = count + 1</code>) to avoid an <em>infinite loop</em>!</li>\n    </ol>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      count = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">1</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">while</span> count &lt;= <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">3</span>:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(count)<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;count = count + <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">1</span>  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Increments so it stops at 4</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}